WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.682
(happy instrumental music)

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.408
- Hi, I'm Hannah.

00:00:15.408 --> 00:00:17.640
I'm your friendly neighborhood wine mom

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.509
and I don't remember why.

00:00:19.509 --> 00:00:22.598
Hi, I'm Hannah, I'm your
friendly neighborhood wine mom

00:00:22.598 --> 00:00:24.088
and if you're anything like me

00:00:24.088 --> 00:00:26.328
you believe that a
glass of wine at nine PM

00:00:26.328 --> 00:00:27.989
makes you a better mom.

00:00:27.989 --> 00:00:30.608
So pour yourself a glass and let's talk.

00:00:30.608 --> 00:00:33.178
But first, here's why
I'm drinking tonight.

00:00:33.178 --> 00:00:35.389
We were at my friend's one-year-old son's

00:00:35.389 --> 00:00:39.979
birthday party last weekend and
my four-year-old son Jackson

00:00:39.979 --> 00:00:42.308
has just decided that
he's not going to point

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.139
with this finger anymore.

00:00:44.139 --> 00:00:45.789
I don't understand why.

00:00:45.789 --> 00:00:48.440
He's four, he's been pointing
like this his whole life.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.628
Anyway, he goes up to
the one-year-old's mom

00:00:51.628 --> 00:00:54.295
and goes, "Hey, is is Noah one?"

00:00:55.438 --> 00:00:56.888
Holding it up.

00:00:56.888 --> 00:00:58.638
The mom is just like,

00:01:01.209 --> 00:01:02.778
so cheers.

00:01:02.778 --> 00:01:05.432
Rose tonight because this was
a birthday present from my mom

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:08.154
and while we're on the topic of birthdays

00:01:08.154 --> 00:01:09.882
let's talk about the best and worst things

00:01:09.882 --> 00:01:14.313
of kids' birthday parties,
about kids' birthday parties.

00:01:14.313 --> 00:01:16.951
Disclaimer, there is not a lot of good.

00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:18.923
Let's start this on a positive note

00:01:18.923 --> 00:01:22.008
with some two really easy
pros, pizza and cake.

00:01:22.008 --> 00:01:24.248
Who doesn't love going
to a kids' birthday party

00:01:24.248 --> 00:01:27.802
and just being able to
wolf down some greasy pizza

00:01:27.802 --> 00:01:30.747
chasing it with like some
awful-ingredient cake?

00:01:30.747 --> 00:01:33.516
And I'm not talking about those artisan

00:01:33.516 --> 00:01:36.933
like beet-colored, prune-sweetened cakes.

00:01:37.949 --> 00:01:41.243
I'm talkin' like the sheet
cake from the grocery store,

00:01:41.243 --> 00:01:43.022
like pump that dye in there.

00:01:43.022 --> 00:01:46.188
If my mouth isn't blue at the
end you haven't done your job.

00:01:46.188 --> 00:01:48.782
But on the other hand,
there are some parents,

00:01:48.782 --> 00:01:51.901
I don't know what kind of
hell they crawled up from.

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.262
(laughing) I probably shouldn't say that.

00:01:53.262 --> 00:01:55.451
They serve salad for the parents.

00:01:55.451 --> 00:01:57.580
What possesses them to do this?

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.931
I'm not a rabbit attending your party.

00:01:59.931 --> 00:02:03.788
I want the same greasy cheese
bread as these children.

00:02:03.788 --> 00:02:06.715
I want to shove my face
full of carbs and fat.

00:02:06.715 --> 00:02:10.222
I don't want leaves and
nuts and berries and shit.

00:02:10.222 --> 00:02:11.468
Pro tip, if.

00:02:11.468 --> 00:02:13.068
(mumbles)

00:02:13.068 --> 00:02:16.942
Pro tip put a billion pieces
of pizza on your kid's plate

00:02:16.942 --> 00:02:19.182
'cause you know eventually
after the third piece

00:02:19.182 --> 00:02:20.957
they're gonna be like,
"Oh my god, I can't."

00:02:20.957 --> 00:02:22.796
And then when they
can't finish it be like,

00:02:22.796 --> 00:02:25.213
"Oh, I don't wanna waste it."

00:02:26.187 --> 00:02:29.539
And then you don't have to be
stuck with your wimpy salad.

00:02:29.539 --> 00:02:32.702
(happy instrumental music)

00:02:32.702 --> 00:02:34.283
I'm drinking this kinda fast.

00:02:34.283 --> 00:02:37.755
Next, alcohol, there are some parents

00:02:37.755 --> 00:02:40.282
probably the same parents who serve salad

00:02:40.282 --> 00:02:44.331
to the other parents who don't
serve booze at their party.

00:02:44.331 --> 00:02:45.692
Why are you doing this to me?

00:02:45.692 --> 00:02:48.538
I didn't come here to drink
some soda with you guys.

00:02:48.538 --> 00:02:51.303
I came here to have a
couple of chugs of wine

00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:54.379
and then even worse if
they don't serve soda

00:02:54.379 --> 00:02:56.218
because they don't want their kids

00:02:56.218 --> 00:02:57.899
to accidentally open a Coca Cola

00:02:57.899 --> 00:02:59.260
and bounce off the fuckin' ceiling.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.089
You're stuck drinking a juice box.

00:03:02.089 --> 00:03:04.791
So I'm standing in the
corner talking to Martha

00:03:04.791 --> 00:03:08.233
about redoing her lawn and at
least if I had a glass of wine

00:03:08.233 --> 00:03:12.600
in my hand I could pretend
to care a little bit more.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.350
I'm out, this rose's really good.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:20.363
The dangers of rose is
it tastes really good

00:03:21.867 --> 00:03:23.962
and it goes down really fast.

00:03:23.962 --> 00:03:28.024
I like write a line on the
bottle when it's time to stop.

00:03:28.024 --> 00:03:30.955
Next is other people's kids.

00:03:30.955 --> 00:03:34.074
Your kid might be awesome,
like both my kids are awesome

00:03:34.074 --> 00:03:35.946
and I'm totally not even biased.

00:03:35.946 --> 00:03:38.379
I'll be the first to
say they're total butts

00:03:38.379 --> 00:03:39.467
but they're awesome.

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:41.195
But when we're at a party

00:03:41.195 --> 00:03:44.825
we also have to deal with
everyone else's crappy kid.

00:03:44.825 --> 00:03:49.464
There's always one giant
kid in the bounce house

00:03:49.464 --> 00:03:52.297
and their parents are
never there watching them,

00:03:52.297 --> 00:03:55.147
they're always off in the
corner rambling to someone

00:03:55.147 --> 00:03:57.323
about their kitchen remodel or something.

00:03:57.323 --> 00:03:59.950
In the meantime, their old, big child

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:02.131
is traumatizing all these two-year-olds

00:04:02.131 --> 00:04:04.150
by like bouncing super big

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:06.338
and making them all fly off the walls

00:04:06.338 --> 00:04:10.505
and it's awkward to try to
tell off this nine-year-old,

00:04:11.522 --> 00:04:13.750
"Hey, can you not be an asshole?"

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.521
On the other hand it makes you realize

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:18.104
that those kids might be shitty

00:04:20.366 --> 00:04:22.948
not as shitty as I thought my kids were.

00:04:22.948 --> 00:04:25.031
(laughs)

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:29.987
They're shitty but not as shitty

00:04:29.987 --> 00:04:32.070
as I thought my kids were

00:04:32.998 --> 00:04:35.818
What am I supposed to say?

00:04:35.818 --> 00:04:37.151
I will get this.

00:04:39.961 --> 00:04:44.668
Sometimes I will admit I think
my kids are totally shitty

00:04:44.668 --> 00:04:47.949
but at least they're not as
shitty as these other kids

00:04:47.949 --> 00:04:48.874
at this party.

00:04:48.874 --> 00:04:50.875
(bells)

00:04:50.875 --> 00:04:52.208
Next, something.

00:04:55.792 --> 00:04:57.290
I'm doin' okay.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:00.348
I need to slow down on the
wine a little bit, okay.

00:05:00.348 --> 00:05:04.478
And finally, hosting
there is so much pressure

00:05:04.478 --> 00:05:06.479
when you're hosting a birthday party

00:05:06.479 --> 00:05:09.305
to one-up the last person's party,

00:05:09.305 --> 00:05:10.797
to go on Pinterest

00:05:10.797 --> 00:05:13.886
and find everything that
you can make yourself.

00:05:13.886 --> 00:05:16.747
If it's not handmade it's
suddenly not as good.

00:05:16.747 --> 00:05:18.750
My attitude is to go to the 99 cent store

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.083
and buy it and save some time.

00:05:22.083 --> 00:05:24.796
It's more like to please the parents,

00:05:24.796 --> 00:05:26.601
which really doesn't make any sense.

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:28.955
I've never been satisfied

00:05:28.955 --> 00:05:30.984
from one my children's birthday parties.

00:05:30.984 --> 00:05:33.146
I've always ended the
birthday party thinking,

00:05:33.146 --> 00:05:35.275
"That was a disaster, that was awful."

00:05:35.275 --> 00:05:37.963
And then I look at my child,

00:05:37.963 --> 00:05:42.330
they don't care if their
cupcake tier was made by hand.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:45.003
They don't care if their
party favors were handmade.

00:05:45.003 --> 00:05:49.003
There's just so much joy
coming from their face,

00:05:50.072 --> 00:05:52.572
just like nothing but pure joy

00:05:52.572 --> 00:05:55.739
and that makes it completely worth it.

00:05:58.368 --> 00:05:59.812
So that's all I got for today.

00:05:59.812 --> 00:06:02.743
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom.

00:06:02.743 --> 00:06:04.289
We have another kids' birthday party

00:06:04.289 --> 00:06:06.455
to attend tomorrow, of course.

00:06:06.455 --> 00:06:08.677
I haven't wrapped the gift, of course.

00:06:08.677 --> 00:06:11.893
So I'm gonna turn this
nice chair into a comfy bed

00:06:11.893 --> 00:06:14.850
and pass right out with
my last two sips of wine.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.789
Until next time.

00:06:16.789 --> 00:06:20.372
(happy instrumental music)

00:06:21.282 --> 00:06:23.282
(belch)

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:26.463
That was so bad.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:32.367
I don't know why they gurgle
every time they come out.

